    "body": "@annevk and @zcorpan, is there any appetite for this one still? I think it would match author expectations and help sync video and `poster > picture` sources as well. \n\nI'm sure I'm overlooking some aspects, but it seems like it could be a relatively small spec change given that the media element load algorithm already exists and it just needs to decide when to run re-selection.\n\nI envision a `react to changes in the environment` like `picture` has that would essentially say.... \n\nWhen a `source` element's `media` attribute state changes to match and that `source` element is earlier in tree order to a currently-selected and still-matching `source` element, or the currently-selected `source` element's `media` no longer matches, save the play-state and time, rerun the media element load algorithm, set the time to saved values.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
