    "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:42:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T16:42:12Z",
    "body": "> Some thoughts: we probably want to be careful with re-selection on window resize, to avoid annoying mid-video reloading or excessive downloads. Probably the most conservative approach would be to **allow re-selecting a video that has not started yet**, but maybe there's a sweet spot that's less conservative and allows upgrading videos on resize etc.\n\nThis made the most sense to me initially on the basis of potential for user-side \"wait, why's it different now\" confusion. My thinking was that user interaction with video could be thought of less like looking at an image in the page layout and more like opening an image in a new tab; I wouldn't want the image source that opens in the new tab to be different from the one I acted on. Once I've hit \"start\" — thinking in terms of full-screen video in particular — I've chosen to \"open\" the video the page presented it to me.\n\nAll that said, after mulling over the nature of the \"different\" for a while, I've come around to the idea of changing the source on-the-fly in line with `picture`. Serving an alternate `video` source requires consideration and effort; presumably nobody would do it unless it served as a legitimate enhancement to the experience.\n\n+1 to carrying over `picture`-like behavior here.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
